Package: sdv
Type: Package
Title: Open R Objects in 'StatDataViewer' from 'RStudio'
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Xiaoguang", "Yan", email = "yanxiaoguang@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An 'RStudio' addin that sends objects from the R session (data
    frames, matrices, tables, vectors, lists, time series, functions, models,
    whole environments and more) to the 'StatDataViewer' desktop application
    <https://statdataviewer.com/>. Each object is converted into a plain
    data frame that the viewer's R data reader can display, or into a text
    document, written to a temporary file and opened in the running viewer.
    Objects can be sent with a keyboard shortcut, from the 'Addins' menu, or
    through View().
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/sashelper/sdv, https://sashelper.r-universe.dev/sdv
BugReports: https://github.com/sashelper/sdv/issues
SystemRequirements: StatDataViewer (macOS or Windows),
    <https://statdataviewer.com/>
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: rstudioapi, stats, utils, methods
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), withr, bit64, zoo, xts
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
